WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.080
With more people living and&nbsp;
working, in and around Rangiora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.960
there's increased pressure on car parking.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:15.840
It's estimated that within the next 30 years&nbsp;
we'll require up to 800 new car parking spaces.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.600
The Council has already bought and leased land&nbsp;
in the town centre here for parking but long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.360
term that's not going to be enough and so we're&nbsp;
looking at constructing a car parked building.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.560
We've already set aside 6 million in&nbsp;
a previous Long Term Plan but we'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.720
need more than that to meet future demand.
 
The council was proposing another 9 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:46.720
dollars from 2028 and that's for a building that's&nbsp;
going to provide up to 280 additional car parks.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.120
Alternatively we could bring forward&nbsp;
funding and build it sooner or defer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.840
the project all together and look at&nbsp;
other options for managing parking.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:11.840
Visit waimakariri.govt.nz/letstalk to take&nbsp;
a look at the options and to have your say.

